  "worked_solution": "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (-8{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1})+C \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =-2{x}^{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
